WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.314
Welcome to OurWater.

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:06.826
After this video you will be able to look at
the weather for an exact place,

00:00:06.946 --> 00:00:10.114
switch between metric and imperial units,

00:00:10.234 --> 00:00:14.650
and know what to do when your signal is weak
and the forecast will not load.

00:00:15.483 --> 00:00:22.851
The grey line shows which place this weather is for:
a name, then two numbers, latitude and longitude.

00:00:23.683 --> 00:00:26.635
To change the place, use this menu.

00:00:26.755 --> 00:00:32.731
It has three ways: your phone's location, a
search by name, or exact coordinates.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:39.646
Every station page lists its own latitude and
longitude, in the box called Station location.

00:00:39.766 --> 00:00:42.358
Here are the numbers for the check dam.

00:00:43.183 --> 00:00:46.423
Back on Weather, choose Enter coordinates.

00:00:46.543 --> 00:00:52.687
Two boxes open: latitude, how far north, and
longitude, how far east.

00:00:53.517 --> 00:00:56.277
First, a mistake on purpose.

00:00:56.397 --> 00:01:00.429
We type ninety-one for latitude, which cannot
be right.

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:03.122
Press Go.

00:01:03.242 --> 00:01:05.378
OurWater does not guess.

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:11.042
It says latitude must be between minus 90 and
90, and leaves the boxes open.

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:16.338
Now the right latitude: twenty-four point six
one five four.

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:19.022
Press Go.

00:01:19.142 --> 00:01:24.110
The grey line shows your exact numbers, and
the page is the weather for that spot.

00:01:24.917 --> 00:01:30.173
Everything below is for this exact spot: the
weather right now, then the week ahead.

00:01:30.983 --> 00:01:33.959
Settings also has Default location.

00:01:34.079 --> 00:01:37.967
It is the place Weather starts with, until you
choose your own.

00:01:38.783 --> 00:01:41.951
The Weather page has no unit switch of its
own.

00:01:42.071 --> 00:01:45.431
It follows Settings, in the card called Units.

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:50.522
Metric means metres, millimetres and degrees
Celsius.

00:01:50.642 --> 00:01:54.794
Imperial means feet, inches and degrees
Fahrenheit.

00:01:55.617 --> 00:01:57.489
Tap Imperial.

00:01:57.609 --> 00:01:59.721
It is saved straight away.

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:05.878
Back on Weather, the same forecast now shows
Fahrenheit, and rain in inches.

00:02:06.683 --> 00:02:09.227
The seven day table follows too.

00:02:09.347 --> 00:02:12.563
Look at the headings: rain now says inch.

00:02:13.383 --> 00:02:16.815
To go back, open Settings and tap Metric.

00:02:17.617 --> 00:02:20.713
Weather is in Celsius and millimetres again.

00:02:21.517 --> 00:02:23.413
Now a weak signal.

00:02:23.533 --> 00:02:26.581
Here we look at the rain gauge by its
coordinates.

00:02:26.701 --> 00:02:31.357
The forecast loads, and OurWater saves a copy
on this device.

00:02:32.183 --> 00:02:36.455
Now imagine your signal drops, as it often
does in the field.

00:02:36.575 --> 00:02:39.431
This line tells you that you are offline.

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:43.538
We ask for the school borewell, close by.

00:02:43.658 --> 00:02:47.618
Same steps: Enter coordinates, then the two
numbers.

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:54.618
OurWater tries a few times, then says plainly
what is wrong: no response from the service.

00:02:54.738 --> 00:02:56.610
Check your connection.

00:02:57.417 --> 00:03:01.665
The last line says it shows the last forecast,
with its age.

00:03:01.785 --> 00:03:04.209
So the page is never empty.

00:03:05.017 --> 00:03:09.049
The saved forecast is still here, boxes and
table.

00:03:09.169 --> 00:03:11.929
It is old weather, so check its age.

00:03:12.049 --> 00:03:14.401
It is kept for one day only.

00:03:15.217 --> 00:03:17.089
Tap Try again.

00:03:17.209 --> 00:03:22.657
The button says Retrying while the page asks
again, and the saved forecast stays.

00:03:23.483 --> 00:03:27.131
Still no signal, so the same message comes
back.

00:03:27.251 --> 00:03:29.123
Nothing is lost.

00:03:29.243 --> 00:03:31.379
Try again whenever you like.

00:03:32.183 --> 00:03:35.279
When the signal is back, tap Try again.

00:03:35.399 --> 00:03:38.999
The warning disappears and the live forecast
returns.

00:03:39.817 --> 00:03:42.889
Leave the page, and come back to My weather.

00:03:43.009 --> 00:03:45.073
The place is still here.

00:03:45.193 --> 00:03:47.545
OurWater remembers it for you.

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:51.350
It is kept on this phone or computer only.

00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:55.142
On another device, set it again with the same
menu.

00:03:55.950 --> 00:04:00.630
That is the Weather page for exact places,
units and a weak signal.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:03.414
Thanks for helping look after our water.
